This statement is added to ensure that the RX ring is re-enabled after processing the received packets. By calling `bcm4908_enet_dma_rx_ring_enable`, it ensures that even if the RX ring was disabled due to a lack of free descriptors, it will be re-enabled, allowing the hardware to continue receiving packets and preventing communication issues.

